-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party models and data (downloaded at install, never vendored)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Model weights are listed with their licences in models/manifest.yaml and the
generated models/LICENSES.md. The attributions below are those that their
licences (CC BY) require when the artifact, or a model trained on it, is
distributed with beepboop.

Speaker embedding: WeSpeaker CAM++ (VoxCeleb), CC BY 4.0
  "wespeaker_en_voxceleb_CAM++" by the WeSpeaker project (wenet-e2e),
  https://github.com/wenet-e2e/wespeaker, trained on VoxCeleb
  (Nagrani et al. 2017; Chung et al. 2018). ONNX export by the sherpa-onnx
  project (k2-fsa, Apache-2.0). Licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

STT test clips: LibriSpeech, CC BY 4.0
  test_wavs/ inside the sherpa-onnx streaming zipformer archive.
  Panayotov et al. 2015, https://www.openslr.org/12/

Text-to-speech: Piper voice en_US-lessac-low
  rhasspy/piper (MIT code), trained on the Blizzard 2013 Lessac corpus,
  https://www.cstr.ed.ac.uk/projects/blizzard/2013/lessac_blizzard2013/license.html
  Research-only provenance, accepted by the owner for this personal/research
  project (D1, ADR 0020). espeak-ng-data (GPL-3.0) ships with the voice and is
  read by the piper-phonemize / espeak-ng phonemiser (GPL-3.0).

Stock "Hey beepboop" wake model (released under Apache-2.0; pending its first
training run). Its full training-data record is
tools/train_wakeword/DATA_LICENSES.md. CC BY 4.0 sources it is trained on:
  - LibriTTS-R (Koizumi et al. 2023), https://www.openslr.org/141/, through the
    rhasspy/piper-sample-generator en_US-libritts_r-medium checkpoint (MIT code;
    fine-tuned from the lessac voice, accepted under D1)
  - LibriSpeech (Panayotov et al. 2015), https://www.openslr.org/12/
  - Google Speech Commands v0.02 (Warden 2018)
  - VOiCES (Richey et al. 2018), https://iqtlabs.github.io/voices/
  - MUSAN (Snyder, Chen, Povey 2015), https://www.openslr.org/17/
  - FSD50K (Fonseca et al. 2022), CC0 and CC BY clips only; per-clip
    Freesound uploader credits are kept in the training metadata
  - Piper voices en_GB-aru-medium (University of Liverpool ARU corpus),
    en_GB-alba-medium (Edinburgh DataShare) and en_GB-vctk-medium (VCTK)
  Apache-2.0: OpenSLR 28 RIRs and noises (Ko et al. 2017).
